id: heran-genes
name: Heran Genes
order: 10
category: body
importance: secondary
# [Any - you decide]: the Saving Throw its Racial Saving Throw Bonus goes to, chosen as it is gained.
choose: savingThrow
description: >
  The blood of conquerors flows through your veins, thanks to the Heran genes infused in your genetic structure.
text: >
  Heran Genes [Any – you decide] (Body): The blood of conquerors flows through your veins, thanks to the Heran genes infused in your genetic structure.
  (1)-[Passive]: Increase your Soak Value by 1(T) while you possess 2+ stacks of Power.
  (2)-[1/Round]: While you are below the Injured Health Threshold, you may use the Power Up Maneuver as an Instant Maneuver.
  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you would use an Attacking Maneuver that possesses an AoE, you may spend up to 2 Adaptation Points to increase the Magnitude of that AoE by 1 Category for each Adaptation Point spent.
  (4)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you would use an Attacking Maneuver that does not possess an AoE, you may spend 2 Adaptation Points to apply a Standard Cone or Line AoE to that Attacking Maneuver.
  (5)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: Lose up to 2 stacks of Power. For every stack of Power lost, gain an Adaptation Point.
---

[passive]
# The Saving Throw named after its name - its Racial Saving Throw Bonus.
allow save.racial.$choice;
# (1)
if (stacksAtLeast(2, "power")) {
    soakValue += 1(T);
}
# (2) An "Instant" button on the Power Up's row while Injured or Critical, once a Round (actor-character-sheet.mjs _onHeranInstant).
allow heranGenes.powerInstant;
# (3), (4) Asked as an Attacking Maneuver is declared, with the Adaptation Points: a Standard Cone or Line for 2 where it has no AoE, 1 or 2
# Magnitudes for as many where it has - once a Round each, Greed of the Hera's way (maneuvers.mjs askBoughtAreas).
allow heranGenes.area;
allow heranGenes.magnitude;

# (5) Your turn begins with Power: how many of up to 2 stacks, asked - an Adaptation Point each (chat.mjs heranGenesTrade). It spends
# Power: no Triggered/Automatic button, ticked on the turn's card (the user's).
[triggered/start-of-turn, chosen, effect 5]
requires hasResource("power");
heranGenesTrade();
